{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>And the sons of Korah did not die.</b> Our Rabbis of blessed memory interpreted: a place was partitioned for them in Gehinnom, and they sat upon it. The place of swallowing, which is the place of judgment, is called Gehinnom; or it may be Gehinnom literally, for the opening of Gehinnom, fixed in the earth, drew near there, according to the view of our Rabbis of blessed memory. And we find that the sons of Korah were singers in the Holy Temple, and this is what is written (Psalms 84:1): ״לבני קרח מזמור״, (ibid. 48): ״שיר מזמור לבני קרח״."], :book :numbers, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:36:14.265044560Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}